r521 (F135). Craig Watson, 24 Oct AWST. Staging (`cdsmnqxtyyoeoznmbidd`) only. Frontend only. No SQL.

Rebased onto live tip r520 (F134), `7ba7e565` (PR #503, customer emails drop the signature and open mailto first). That release keeps r520 / F134. This Booking change was drafted as r520 / F134 before that squash-merge landed, and is renumbered to the next free pair, r521 / F135.

## What was wrong

Vehicle Locations, Booking column, preferred this wording when the row had `pilbaraServiceJobCard`:

`Pilbara Service Review · R/O loaded`

That flag means the row has one Pilbara service job card. It is not a separate kind of vehicle. The badge was chosen ahead of Imported by email, Navision source and Shared sync pending, so the Booking column showed a neutral source badge instead of the same text as any other vehicle in the same state.

Book all stations already deleted that wording when the vehicle was eligible to book. This release stops emitting it.

## What changed

`incomingVehicleDetailRow` no longer reads the job-card flag for the Booking column. The read-only reasons are unchanged: identity conflict, imported by email, Navision source, shared sync pending.

An eligible vehicle (controller or administrator, canonical id and version, no identity conflict, location authority ready, active and on the board, location PMB, yard hold, or in transit with a Kewdale ETA) gets Book all stations, the same control as any other eligible vehicle.

A vehicle that is not eligible keeps the same source badge it would have without the flag. Stock 13018393 (job card J139125903, Dept 139, `current_location` Other, ETA 2026-11-10) is in that group because location Other is not a workshop booking location. Its Booking column no longer says Pilbara Service Review · R/O loaded.

Cache bust `r521=2026.10.24.r521` on app.js. styles.css untouched. Department 135 / Karratha stays frozen.

## Undo

Revert this PR. Nothing to undo in the database.
